2. v9 ThermalProfile unification (#215)
   - 5 byte-identical *ThermalProfile classes (NPU/CGRA/DPU/TPU/DSP)
     collapse to a single aliased type in compute_block_common.
   - CPU + GPU stay separate (legitimate architectural divergence:
     per-cluster ClockDomain on CPU; ClockDomain + memory_clock +
     native_acceleration on GPU).
   - KPU deferred to v11+ (doubly-purposed as chip-level Power).
   - Net -179 LOC.

3. v10 OnDieFabric unification (#217)
   - First INHERITANCE-based unification (vs v8/v9 alias-based).
     Reason: topology enum is architecture-specific (CPU's
     infinity_fabric, DPU's aie_mesh, NPU's systolic). Shared base
     in compute_block_common carries the 7 shared fields + optional
     mesh dims + optional confidence; per-kind subclasses add only
     topology.
   - CPU 'stop_count' and GPU 'controller_count' renamed to
     unit_count, matching the 4-of-6 convention. 3 YAMLs updated
     atomically (intel_core_i7_12700k + 2 Jetson AGX).
   - Schema-only -92 LOC; subclass bodies shrink from ~25-30 LOC
     to ~5 LOC.

4. v11 DRAM-attachment naming reconciliation (#219)
   - CGRA's has_host_dram/host_dram_* renamed to has_external_dram/
